{
 "id": "D-18 B8 (handoff-turn, handoff-state, dispatch --handoff-ht)",
 "note": "D-18 §9.1 / B3 / B8 (core half of HT-LT-01..03). handoff-turn open exclusive-creates <watch>/<sid>/handoff-turn/<ht>.json (0600, row handoff_turn_open) and answers EXISTS for a taken ht; handoff-state prints none / staged <stage> draft=<0|1> finish=<publish command, no session id> / published <path> / superseded <nonce>; supersede needs an open ht. The lib seams begin and publish call: the open ht is the newest with no .published and at most 60 min old; one stage and one published handoff per ht. handoff-turn close --why cancelled|ended exclusive-creates <ht>.closed (0600; ok, EXISTS, REFUSED: no-ht exit 3 for an unknown ht), begin no longer binds that ht and handoff-state does not change (CR-F17/F25). A <ht>.published claim counts as published only when its path is a regular file whose last line is the sentinel of the stage nonce, else handoff-state prints publish-failed <path> (CR-F9). dispatch --handoff-ht puts handoff_ht in the record and the row, and the tag handoff is accepted",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
